Their output is a finished sequence of known size, so it is indistinguishable from a fresh source
and splitting can start again after it:
`map f .sort by .limit 10000 .filter g .list`
is two parallel regions with one fence in between.
Crucially if a fence operation is at the beginning or directly after another fence, some optimisations are possible.

